<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n37625" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">praefurnĭum</span></b> , i, n.
		prae-furnus. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>The opening of a furnace</i>, <i>the
				door</i> by which fuel is admitted: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">si uno praefurnio coques,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cato, R. R. 38, 1</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>The heating-room</i>, or hot anteroom of a bath, =
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">προπνιγεῖον</span>, <i><span class="en">Vitr. 5,
				10, 2</span></i>; <i><span class="en">7,
			10</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
